8. Accounts and license verification
You must provide accurate information where required for licensing and protect your credentials against unauthorized use. Notify us promptly if you reasonably believe your account or license has been compromised.
The Software may require internet access and periodic license verification. Verification failures, expired entitlements, or service interruptions may affect access to licensed functionality, subject to applicable law and the commitments made when your entitlement was supplied.
Protected releases use account-linked personalization for license enforcement and investigation of unauthorized redistribution. Personalized encrypted implementation bundles are linked to your licensed account, machine identifier, install key and client build. These identifiers are not a visible on-screen watermark. A redistributed encrypted bundle can be associated with its licensed account; this does not establish who redistributed it.
Protected releases also check local JVM agent flags and, on Linux, known agent-library mappings. An unsupported instrumented runtime is refused. Detected integrity failures erase runtime protection keys and require an intact client and a fresh process. This does not delete your files or license.
Processing of personal data, including authentication, personalization and fraud-prevention identifiers, is described in our separate Privacy Notice: https://larpclient.com/privacy. This Agreement does not itself constitute consent to processing that requires separate consent.
